35,2,1,talk,Servas,,"The technicians are gone, yet the glasshouse crew remains strong. We must weigh this carefully before deciding.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Sakura,,"Whoa! Free computing hours? That’s huge! But animal costs jumped way up. So, fancy simulations are cheap, but keeping animals happy is expensive now!","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I found that catalogue projects still help people years later, but mechanism ones often stall. Also, breeding colonies cause double the delays.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"Eleven weeks idle on the spectroscopy suite. That’s a massive bottleneck. Plus, breeding colonies cause double the delays. We need to avoid live animal risks.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Minako,,"The repository migration is complete; deposits now clear in weeks, not years. However, the spectroscopy suite sat idle for eleven weeks.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Servas,,"The modelling analysts are gone until autumn, yet the glasshouse crew stands firm. This imbalance shapes what we can truly support.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Takumi, wait! If simulations are free, maybe the spectroscopy delay doesn't matter as much? I'm still confused about the animal costs though!","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I am worried. If mechanism studies stall, and breeding causes delays, we must be very careful.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Sakura, free compute doesn't fix broken hardware. The suite is dead. @Minako, confirm the spectroscopy outage is still active?","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Sakura"",""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Takumi, the outage was last year. The suite is operational now, though staffing remains thin.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Servas,,"The glasshouse crew is ready, but the modelling minds are absent. We must choose a path that matches our current hands.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Sakura,,"@Minako, so the glasshouse is booked solid? That means the free compute is useless if we can’t even get bench space!","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I agree. The data shows mechanism-focused work often stalls. We should prioritize projects that don't rely on those risky, delayed elements.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
